<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24125" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-tempĕrātus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>untempered</i>, <i>inclement.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quid ad caeli naturam intemperatius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Helv. 6</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hence: intemperatum vinum,</span>”
				<i>unmixed wine</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael. Aur. Acut. 3, 17, §
				158</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>immoderate</i>, <i>intemperate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">benevolentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Lael. 20</span></i>
			.— <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intempĕ-rātē</span></b> ,
				<i>intemperately</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immoderate et intemperate vivere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Univ. 12</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
